## Highlights
 Collagen was extracted from bigeye tuna byproducts using acetic acid and pepsin The acid-soluble and pepsin-soluble collagen in skin were 13.5 and $16.7\%$ All the extracted collagens were type I collagen Physiochemical properties of fish collagen were comparable to mammalian collagen Bigeye tuna collagen can be used as an alternate of mammalian collagen
